    <Placemark>
      <name>Qatna (קטנה)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Qatna (קטנה)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 4: International Comparative Site (&lt; 100m - 1km)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Syria</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.5 (Pages 81)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>During Middle Bronze Age II, a spring was enclosed within the walls of the kingdom city of Qatna, while a stream outside the rampart may have filled a moat for defense.</p>]]></description>
