    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Dan (תל דן)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Dan (תל דן)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Spring Cave Capture</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Upper Galilee</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.2 (Pages 73, 74, 75)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>The city of Dan, enclosed by a massive rampart, incorporated the eastern springs of Dan within its fortifications during the Middle Bronze Age, serving as the primary water source. An artificial water passage (sinkhole) was likely constructed concurrently with the rampart to manage excess water.</p>]]></description>
