    <Placemark>
      <name>Tel Megiddo (תל מגידו)</name>
      <description><![CDATA[<h3>Tel Megiddo (תל מגידו)</h3>
<p><b>Period:</b> 06. Middle Bronze Age (MB) (-2200 to -1550 BCE)</p>
<p><b>Installation Type:</b> Water Tunnel Shaft</p>
<p><b>Location Precision:</b> Tier 1: High Precision (Pinpoint Well/Installation &lt; 50m)</p>
<p><b>Region:</b> Jezreel Valley</p>
<p><b>Dissertation Reference:</b> §2.6.8 (Pages 87)</p>
<hr/>
<p><b>Archaeological Description (06. Middle Bronze Age):</b></p>
<p>A large depression in the northern part of the tel is hypothesized to be an early water system (MB, LB, possibly EB) reaching groundwater, potentially connected to Ein el-Qubi.</p>]]></description>
